1
00:00:00,270 --> 00:00:01,710
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,710 --> 00:00:03,110
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:05,310
(Episode 11)

4
00:00:13,050 --> 00:00:15,420
She is drowning in debt.
What money could she possibly have?

5
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:20,130
If she signed the divorce papers
and split up,

6
00:00:20,990 --> 00:00:22,730
she should just focus
on living her own life.

7
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:27,300
Yes, she is too soft-hearted,

8
00:00:28,730 --> 00:00:30,970
which is why she lived
with my foolish son for so long.

9
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:35,570
How much is this anyway?

10
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:38,610
She must have paid
at least 50 dollars for it.

11
00:00:41,650 --> 00:00:42,680
Goodness.

12
00:00:44,620 --> 00:00:45,920
Just wait until I see her.

13
00:00:46,790 --> 00:00:48,520
I am going to smack her on the back.

14
00:00:52,790 --> 00:00:53,790
Mom.

15
00:00:56,490 --> 00:00:57,660
Mom, I am coming in.

16
00:00:58,100 --> 00:00:59,460
Coming in where? Don't you dare.

17
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:01,070
This is my room.

18
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:03,470
What is wrong, Mom?

19
00:01:05,270 --> 00:01:06,300
Mom.

20
00:01:08,810 --> 00:01:10,740
Enough with the "Mom, Mom."

21
00:01:12,740 --> 00:01:15,450
Stop calling me that, you brats.

22
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:21,020
Mom, I am coming in.

23
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:28,660
Where are you going?

24
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:37,740
Are you not even worried
about your brother's wife?

25
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:41,170
Even if you are up to your neck
in your own problems, you jerk,

26
00:01:41,570 --> 00:01:42,910
since you are living at home...

27
00:01:43,510 --> 00:01:46,240
and seeing your brother and Su Ah
every morning and evening,

28
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:48,850
how can you not even ask
where your brother's wife went...

29
00:01:48,980 --> 00:01:50,010
or how she is doing?

30
00:01:53,180 --> 00:01:54,450
If I ask,

31
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:56,450
does it solve anything?

32
00:01:57,620 --> 00:02:00,190
So if it does not solve anything,
you are not even going to care?

33
00:02:01,090 --> 00:02:02,660
You are so cold-hearted.

34
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:05,530
I always knew
you only cared about yourself...

35
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:07,230
ever since you were little.

36
00:02:07,370 --> 00:02:09,370
You should not treat
your brother's wife like this.

37
00:02:09,900 --> 00:02:12,900
Grandma's holding a Yut game
tonight anyway, right?

38
00:02:13,640 --> 00:02:14,670
Scold me then.

39
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:18,640
Right, so what do you want?

40
00:02:19,880 --> 00:02:20,910
I am busy.

41
00:02:21,410 --> 00:02:23,210
Da Mi found out where
your brother's wife is living.

42
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:24,280
I am going to go see her.

43
00:02:29,620 --> 00:02:30,720
Could you get some money...

44
00:02:32,060 --> 00:02:33,460
together for me?

45
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:36,830
If I want to have
an easier time at work right now,

46
00:02:36,900 --> 00:02:38,530
I need to pay off
my urgent debts first.

47
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:43,300
You're the only one
who can help, Mom.

48
00:02:44,740 --> 00:02:47,240
Who was it that blew
the Officetel I got for you?

49
00:02:48,970 --> 00:02:54,350
- I do not have any money.
- You must have money saved up...

50
00:02:54,450 --> 00:02:56,510
to help me buy an apartment
when I get married, right?

51
00:02:57,850 --> 00:02:58,920
Look at this guy.

52
00:02:59,580 --> 00:03:01,720
Sure, I did that for your brother.

53
00:03:02,220 --> 00:03:03,560
But not for you.

54
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:05,520
Wait, why not?

55
00:03:05,590 --> 00:03:08,260
Between academies, tutoring,
and studying abroad,

56
00:03:08,460 --> 00:03:10,160
do you know how much money
I spent supporting you?

57
00:03:11,060 --> 00:03:14,530
And the officetel you blew away
was bought with Grandma's help.

58
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:16,000
Know your facts before you speak.

59
00:03:16,630 --> 00:03:19,240
Out of my three children,
you took and spent the most money.

60
00:03:19,540 --> 00:03:21,570
What? Apartment funds?

61
00:03:22,540 --> 00:03:24,280
If you had just worked diligently
at your company,

62
00:03:24,340 --> 00:03:25,480
you'd have bought
a 66-meter-squre apartment...

63
00:03:25,510 --> 00:03:26,780
with money left over.

64
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:29,880
Then...

65
00:03:31,250 --> 00:03:33,320
I will earn money
and pay you back later, so...

66
00:03:33,990 --> 00:03:35,820
even the money you saved
for Da Mi...

67
00:03:37,660 --> 00:03:38,820
Please lend it to me, Mom.

68
00:03:39,690 --> 00:03:41,590
You have completely lost your mind.

69
00:03:43,630 --> 00:03:45,860
Where did my smart and successful
second son go?

70
00:03:46,460 --> 00:03:47,830
You want me to take Da Mi's money?

71
00:03:52,040 --> 00:03:53,070
Your youngest sister's?

72
00:03:54,410 --> 00:03:55,770
She has been working
at the department store,

73
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:57,280
so she must have saved quite a bit.

74
00:03:58,340 --> 00:04:00,310
You raised her well all this time,
is that not enough?

75
00:04:00,950 --> 00:04:04,280
You do not need to help her
with her marriage funds.

76
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:09,390
And honestly, Da Mi is
not even your biological daughter.

77
00:04:10,760 --> 00:04:11,790
Will you shut your mouth?

78
00:04:14,990 --> 00:04:16,030
Mom.

79
00:04:17,260 --> 00:04:18,630
A spoiled child...

80
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:21,630
becomes a scoundrel in an instant.

81
00:04:23,270 --> 00:04:24,740
What is so great
about that darn money?

82
00:04:39,020 --> 00:04:40,390
Wait, did I say something wrong?

83
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:42,850
I am just saying I will borrow it
because it is urgent,

84
00:04:42,920 --> 00:04:44,160
and I will pay it back later,
so why?

85
00:04:45,020 --> 00:04:46,760
I am about to die right now.

86
00:04:47,290 --> 00:04:48,330
I mean, why?

87
00:04:50,030 --> 00:04:51,200
Is she really my mother?

88
00:04:56,770 --> 00:04:58,170
When you watch things like dramas,

89
00:04:58,270 --> 00:05:01,610
the elevator always breaks down
at least once in times like this.

90
00:05:02,070 --> 00:05:04,380
Then I would tremble in fear,

91
00:05:04,910 --> 00:05:07,180
and Team Leader Cha
would comfort me...

92
00:05:07,250 --> 00:05:09,510
by holding
my trembling body tightly.

93
00:05:12,180 --> 00:05:13,180
Break down.

94
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:16,990
Please break down, elevator, okay?

95
00:05:27,130 --> 00:05:29,200
That is because you only see her
as a subordinate.

96
00:05:29,270 --> 00:05:31,170
Try looking at her as a woman.

97
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:35,770
At least make an effort. Do Yun,
it is your mother's request. Okay?

98
00:05:37,710 --> 00:05:38,710
Assistant Manager Kang?

99
00:05:39,010 --> 00:05:40,210
Yes, Team Leader Cha.

100
00:05:41,310 --> 00:05:43,310
Is there a reason
you have to wear your collar...

101
00:05:43,450 --> 00:05:44,550
so open like that?

102
00:05:45,450 --> 00:05:46,450
Excuse me?

103
00:05:49,050 --> 00:05:54,030
This is just because wearing it
like this looks stylish, and also...

104
00:05:54,330 --> 00:05:55,460
From my perspective,

105
00:05:55,630 --> 00:05:58,600
buttoning 1 or 2 more buttons
would look much more stylish.

106
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:00,930
It would also be more comfortable
for people of all ages to look at.

107
00:06:01,170 --> 00:06:04,100
This is strictly interest and advice
from a superior.

108
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:06,270
I apologize if it offends you.

109
00:06:07,540 --> 00:06:08,570
Not at all.

110
00:06:14,310 --> 00:06:16,410
- Hey, they are here.
- You guys go in first.

111
00:06:16,450 --> 00:06:18,980
- They are here.
- Do not push. What are you doing?

112
00:06:19,050 --> 00:06:20,850
- Seriously. Come in, come in.
- Come in quickly.

113
00:06:23,020 --> 00:06:24,920
- What is this, seriously?
- Do not push.

114
00:06:25,060 --> 00:06:27,160
- Please be quiet.
- I really saw it.

115
00:06:27,390 --> 00:06:28,390
What are you doing?

116
00:06:29,060 --> 00:06:30,760
The garden is decorated
really well, too.

117
00:06:31,100 --> 00:06:32,160
Hey, do not push.

118
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:34,800
- I can do what I want.
- Hey, stay still, seriously.

119
00:06:34,870 --> 00:06:36,170
What are you doing? Take it out.

120
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:40,200
I said stop it.
What's wrong with you?

121
00:06:40,940 --> 00:06:42,470
This is so annoying.

122
00:06:42,810 --> 00:06:43,880
I'm serious...

123
00:06:43,980 --> 00:06:45,180
Can you answer the phone
if it rings?

124
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:46,540
We're almost out of time.

125
00:06:46,540 --> 00:06:48,450
- Why?
- I'm saying go up all at once.

126
00:06:48,610 --> 00:06:49,950
- Is it pretty?
- Is it really okay?

127
00:06:50,010 --> 00:06:51,180
- It's really good.
- Is it okay?

128
00:06:51,250 --> 00:06:52,380
- This is crazy.
- Let's go.

129
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:58,360
- What's wrong?
- Hey, what's wrong?

130
00:07:10,670 --> 00:07:13,500
- I don't know, it's not.
- Geun Woo, let's go.

131
00:07:16,370 --> 00:07:17,980
What? It's the first floor.

132
00:07:33,220 --> 00:07:36,030
Yes, Mom.
I'm a little busy right now.

133
00:07:36,830 --> 00:07:39,660
No matter how much I think about it,
this isn't right, sweetie.

134
00:07:39,730 --> 00:07:40,730
What is it this time?

135
00:07:42,030 --> 00:07:43,470
I'm talking about this sofa.

136
00:07:44,070 --> 00:07:46,000
I went all the way to the
Nonhyeon-dong furniture street...

137
00:07:46,070 --> 00:07:48,970
to score this,
waited a whopping four months,

138
00:07:49,070 --> 00:07:50,810
and finally brought it
into my space.

139
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:53,850
But your dad says...

140
00:07:53,910 --> 00:07:55,350
we should throw it away
when we move.

141
00:07:55,410 --> 00:07:56,910
Does that make any sense?

142
00:07:57,650 --> 00:07:59,920
I know how you feel, Mom.

143
00:08:00,550 --> 00:08:03,960
But shouldn't that change
depending on the situation?

144
00:08:04,690 --> 00:08:05,690
What?

145
00:08:06,120 --> 00:08:07,730
Your feelings, I mean.

146
00:08:09,230 --> 00:08:11,130
Are you telling me
to throw it away? Me?

147
00:08:11,560 --> 00:08:13,830
There are a lot of cheap
and good ones these days.

148
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:16,100
Later on, I'll buy you something...

149
00:08:16,730 --> 00:08:19,000
that will more than satisfy you, Mom.

150
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:20,610
Is that okay?

151
00:08:22,810 --> 00:08:24,510
I'm busy.
I have a lot of work to do.

152
00:08:24,640 --> 00:08:25,640
I'll see you at home, Mom.

153
00:08:27,180 --> 00:08:28,780
That's my girl.

154
00:08:29,010 --> 00:08:31,450
Who gave birth to
Assistant Manager Kang Ye Ri?

155
00:08:31,520 --> 00:08:33,380
This Park Ji Young did.

156
00:08:33,950 --> 00:08:36,250
Get back to work. I love you.

157
00:08:36,650 --> 00:08:39,020
I live only for my daughter.

158
00:08:47,030 --> 00:08:50,370
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

159
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:51,670
Ri Ja.

160
00:08:52,100 --> 00:08:54,870
This isn't all the makgeolli
we have in stock, is it?

161
00:08:55,740 --> 00:08:58,280
- Why, Mrs. Choi?
- Well, I wanted to stock up...

162
00:08:58,410 --> 00:08:59,640
and take some home.

163
00:09:00,850 --> 00:09:04,120
- How many bottles?
- Yes, 20 bottles.

164
00:09:05,580 --> 00:09:07,150
Twenty?

165
00:09:09,450 --> 00:09:10,450
Twenty bottles.

166
00:09:19,130 --> 00:09:20,670
- Hey.
- You startled me.

167
00:09:20,730 --> 00:09:24,240
Who pays with cash these days?
Everyone uses cards now.

168
00:09:24,900 --> 00:09:27,870
You can't rob the register
like you used to.

169
00:09:27,940 --> 00:09:29,540
Dream on.

170
00:09:30,110 --> 00:09:32,810
Auntie. How old do you think I am?

171
00:09:33,340 --> 00:09:35,810
And if anyone heard you,
they'd think I was a robber.

172
00:09:36,010 --> 00:09:37,450
Just because I took a little...

173
00:09:37,520 --> 00:09:38,950
when I didn't have
enough allowance as a kid.

174
00:09:39,580 --> 00:09:40,590
Hey.

175
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:44,160
Did you hear what Grandma just said?

176
00:09:44,460 --> 00:09:45,460
What?

177
00:09:46,090 --> 00:09:49,030
I think she said something
about rice wine?

178
00:09:49,860 --> 00:09:52,730
She wants us to prepare
20 bottles this time,

179
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:53,800
can you believe it?

180
00:09:54,370 --> 00:09:56,830
You are the only one in this house
who causes trouble.

181
00:09:57,640 --> 00:09:59,470
I have no idea what is going on.

182
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:03,070
Do you happen to know anything?

183
00:10:03,470 --> 00:10:04,910
I am not sure.

184
00:10:05,510 --> 00:10:09,550
It seemed like Dae Chi
had something on his mind.

185
00:10:10,150 --> 00:10:12,180
What kind of problem
could he possibly have?

186
00:10:14,150 --> 00:10:15,150
Oh, right.

187
00:10:15,820 --> 00:10:19,590
- I heard he got a girl in trouble.
- Then that is great news.

188
00:10:19,820 --> 00:10:22,390
Grandma and Mom are so anxious
to get him married off.

189
00:10:23,330 --> 00:10:25,630
That is true.

190
00:10:30,100 --> 00:10:31,200
Seriously.

191
00:10:36,140 --> 00:10:37,140
Here.

192
00:10:37,780 --> 00:10:39,180
Thank you, Auntie.

193
00:10:48,290 --> 00:10:49,850
When did I put this here?

194
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:01,370
Oh my.

195
00:11:01,930 --> 00:11:03,500
This is totally my style.

196
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:08,070
Excuse me, ma'am?

197
00:11:09,710 --> 00:11:11,210
I am sorry.

198
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:12,610
This belongs to you,
Manager Kang, right?

199
00:11:12,910 --> 00:11:14,350
Yes, it does.

200
00:11:14,450 --> 00:11:16,010
Your tablet is exactly
the same as mine.

201
00:11:16,450 --> 00:11:17,820
We must have a real connection.

202
00:11:17,880 --> 00:11:19,120
Even the password pattern
is the same.

203
00:11:19,950 --> 00:11:23,190
So I naturally thought it was mine
and opened it.

204
00:11:24,160 --> 00:11:25,290
Your payment is complete.

205
00:11:28,030 --> 00:11:32,000
- Are you upset?
- I am not exactly upset,

206
00:11:32,160 --> 00:11:33,530
just a little caught off guard.

207
00:11:36,470 --> 00:11:37,470
Just sit down for a second.

208
00:11:48,410 --> 00:11:49,410
See?

209
00:11:50,350 --> 00:11:52,050
My pattern is exactly
the same as yours.

210
00:11:52,680 --> 00:11:56,320
- Look, I am not lying.
- You are right.

211
00:11:56,590 --> 00:11:57,820
It is the exact same model, too.

212
00:11:59,060 --> 00:12:01,060
Your goal is to become
a fashion designer, right?

213
00:12:02,090 --> 00:12:05,360
My dream and goal is to launch
my own lingerie brand.

214
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:08,030
But I do not have any money.

215
00:12:08,770 --> 00:12:10,100
You do not have any money?

216
00:12:10,770 --> 00:12:12,340
Just based on
what you bought today...

217
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:14,610
I told you, it's my brother's card.

218
00:12:15,610 --> 00:12:16,610
Here, look.

219
00:12:18,410 --> 00:12:21,910
I poured my blood, sweat, tears,
and even my soul...

220
00:12:22,350 --> 00:12:23,410
into all of these designs.

221
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:25,320
What do you think?

222
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:26,950
Well...

223
00:12:27,720 --> 00:12:29,720
They are flashy and eye-catching.

224
00:12:30,750 --> 00:12:32,820
And to be completely honest...

225
00:12:34,020 --> 00:12:36,390
Are they too revealing?
Do they look cheap?

226
00:12:37,190 --> 00:12:38,730
No, it is not that.

227
00:12:41,470 --> 00:12:44,030
It is not lingerie meant
to impress someone else,

228
00:12:44,100 --> 00:12:47,270
but rather a kind of beauty
solely for the woman wearing it.

229
00:12:47,940 --> 00:12:51,080
The passion to look beautiful,
and the inner desires.

230
00:12:51,780 --> 00:12:53,710
I can see all of that,
which makes it look sexy.

231
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:55,250
In a classy way.

232
00:12:57,280 --> 00:13:00,450
You're not just saying that
because I'm a VIP customer, right?

233
00:13:01,520 --> 00:13:04,020
I don't sit side by side
with VIP customers...

234
00:13:04,090 --> 00:13:07,190
and have personal chats like this.
It's against the rules.

235
00:13:07,990 --> 00:13:10,330
Then I guess I have to believe you.

236
00:13:11,100 --> 00:13:12,300
The design is great,

237
00:13:12,360 --> 00:13:14,370
so you just need
to use good materials.

238
00:13:14,830 --> 00:13:15,870
Maybe we could even see the birth...

239
00:13:15,930 --> 00:13:19,170
of a brand like Victoria's Secret
right here in our country.

240
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:22,340
Thank you, Manager Kang.

241
00:13:23,110 --> 00:13:26,080
Your designs are truly excellent.
They're really cool.

242
00:13:27,210 --> 00:13:29,010
Maybe our connection...

243
00:13:29,810 --> 00:13:31,420
No, maybe it's destiny.

244
00:13:32,450 --> 00:13:34,220
Destiny is a bit much.

245
00:13:34,290 --> 00:13:35,690
(K Department Store)

246
00:13:40,160 --> 00:13:41,830
Welcome, sir.

247
00:13:43,630 --> 00:13:44,760
Yes.

248
00:13:45,700 --> 00:13:49,070
What are you doing here?
Shouldn't you be at work right now?

249
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,040
Are you out of your mind?

250
00:13:55,240 --> 00:13:56,840
How could you spend 30,000 dollars
all at once?

251
00:13:57,640 --> 00:13:59,980
Who told me I could spend
whatever I wanted?

252
00:14:00,640 --> 00:14:02,550
You chased me all the way here
just for that?

253
00:14:06,280 --> 00:14:07,280
Just get up.

254
00:14:07,990 --> 00:14:09,120
Get up, let's go.

255
00:14:09,820 --> 00:14:12,820
Sir, since you're here,
would you like some tea?

256
00:14:14,090 --> 00:14:15,990
No, thanks. We're in a hurry,
so we'll be going.

257
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:19,130
Aren't you getting up? Hurry.

258
00:14:19,860 --> 00:14:21,330
Got it.

259
00:14:22,530 --> 00:14:23,530
Let's go.

260
00:14:25,700 --> 00:14:28,470
Manager Kang, please have the bag
delivered to my house...

261
00:14:28,540 --> 00:14:30,110
once all the clothes are altered.

262
00:14:33,440 --> 00:14:34,450
See you again.

263
00:14:37,580 --> 00:14:39,380
Thank you. Have a good day.

264
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:45,860
Those siblings are totally
Tom and Jerry, aren't they?

265
00:14:48,090 --> 00:14:49,090
I know.

266
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:06,480
(Hwanggeum Capital)

267
00:15:21,090 --> 00:15:22,090
Yes, give it to me.

268
00:15:23,660 --> 00:15:24,730
That's enough.

269
00:15:31,840 --> 00:15:33,440
Hello, Madam Chairwoman.

270
00:15:35,670 --> 00:15:36,670
Welcome, Mother.

271
00:15:38,040 --> 00:15:40,440
Am I a mob boss?

272
00:15:41,080 --> 00:15:43,350
Who told you to do this nonsense?

273
00:15:43,910 --> 00:15:46,250
Get back inside. Do your work.

274
00:15:51,460 --> 00:15:55,790
Goodness, you really don't
listen, do you?

275
00:15:56,730 --> 00:15:58,860
With company discipline like this.

276
00:16:02,530 --> 00:16:03,530
Is she lucid?

277
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:04,800
Yes.

278
00:16:08,770 --> 00:16:09,770
(CEO Jeon Jin Hee)

279
00:16:09,870 --> 00:16:11,510
(Hwanggeum Apparel)

280
00:16:11,910 --> 00:16:12,980
What's going on?

281
00:16:13,810 --> 00:16:15,450
Se Na, why are you at the office?

282
00:16:16,310 --> 00:16:18,320
I don't know, he dragged me here.

283
00:16:18,920 --> 00:16:21,550
Mom, you said you reduced
her credit card limit.

284
00:16:22,120 --> 00:16:24,020
So I lent her my card,
and guess what...

285
00:16:24,460 --> 00:16:26,460
She spent 30,000 dollars
at the luxury goods section today.

286
00:16:26,920 --> 00:16:29,260
- Are you just going to let her be?
- Is this true?

287
00:16:29,430 --> 00:16:31,530
He told me I could spend
whatever I wanted.

288
00:16:31,600 --> 00:16:32,600
Even so.

289
00:16:34,330 --> 00:16:35,470
Did you take the card back?

290
00:16:36,430 --> 00:16:37,430
Yes.

291
00:16:38,840 --> 00:16:41,110
For now, go home and stay put.

292
00:16:41,970 --> 00:16:43,510
Today, there is an event
for students...

293
00:16:43,510 --> 00:16:45,510
sponsored by
the scholarship foundation.

294
00:16:45,940 --> 00:16:47,640
You need to go and give
a congratulatory speech.

295
00:16:47,810 --> 00:16:49,380
Let us talk when you get home, son.

296
00:16:49,680 --> 00:16:50,750
Yes, I understand.

297
00:16:51,450 --> 00:16:53,250
Mom, I have something to tell you...

298
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:55,550
- about him too.
- What is it?

299
00:16:56,020 --> 00:16:57,450
You know what, Mom? Do Yun...

300
00:16:57,550 --> 00:16:59,960
is totally obsessed with that woman,
Manager Kang at the luxury boutique.

301
00:17:00,590 --> 00:17:03,260
That is why he chased after me today
when I was swiping the card.

302
00:17:04,700 --> 00:17:05,730
Obsessed?

303
00:17:06,330 --> 00:17:08,470
You mean you are interested
in her as a woman?

304
00:17:09,570 --> 00:17:10,770
Not at all, Mom.

305
00:17:11,240 --> 00:17:13,340
Se Na is just being delusional.
It is absolutely not true.

306
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:15,040
Sure it's not.

307
00:17:15,310 --> 00:17:17,140
If I spent 30,000 dollars
on the card,

308
00:17:17,210 --> 00:17:19,110
you could have just canceled it
right then and there.

309
00:17:19,480 --> 00:17:21,010
Why would you go all the way
to the boutique...

310
00:17:21,080 --> 00:17:22,680
during your working hours?

311
00:17:23,180 --> 00:17:25,180
You were thinking about her
and wanted to see her again,

312
00:17:25,350 --> 00:17:27,050
so your feet just carried you there,
did they not?

313
00:17:27,120 --> 00:17:28,120
Hey.

314
00:17:28,850 --> 00:17:30,990
That was because
I was so dumbfounded and angry...

315
00:17:31,050 --> 00:17:32,920
Exactly, you moved
without even realizing it.

316
00:17:33,620 --> 00:17:35,790
That is how
a one-sided crush begins.

317
00:17:36,190 --> 00:17:38,200
Se Na, you hurry up and go home.

318
00:17:40,660 --> 00:17:41,670
Do Yun.

319
00:17:42,170 --> 00:17:43,700
It really is not true.

320
00:17:44,230 --> 00:17:46,870
Okay. I hope it is not true either.

321
00:17:52,410 --> 00:17:55,580
- Seriously.
- That hurts.

322
00:17:56,280 --> 00:17:57,350
Gosh.

323
00:17:58,050 --> 00:18:00,550
By the way Do Yun, our family
is super rich, right?

324
00:18:00,850 --> 00:18:02,320
So why do we not
spend our money freely?

325
00:18:03,120 --> 00:18:04,920
To help stimulate the local economy,

326
00:18:04,990 --> 00:18:06,790
people like us should be allowed
to spend a lot.

327
00:18:06,990 --> 00:18:09,290
Try saying that exact same thing
in front of Grandma.

328
00:18:09,530 --> 00:18:10,860
If you are confident
she will not kick you out.

329
00:18:11,760 --> 00:18:15,900
You heard Mom, right?
Be a good girl and go straight home.

330
00:18:28,810 --> 00:18:30,780
(Hwanggeum Capital)

331
00:18:30,850 --> 00:18:32,820
(CEO Cha In Sung)

332
00:18:35,190 --> 00:18:37,320
What brings you all the way
to the office?

333
00:18:39,090 --> 00:18:41,860
Do you want to step down
from your position as CEO?

334
00:18:42,590 --> 00:18:44,560
You must be tired of being
the CEO by now, right?

335
00:18:45,400 --> 00:18:46,930
Well, if you do not want
to do it, step down.

336
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:48,370
Even without you,

337
00:18:48,630 --> 00:18:50,600
there are plenty of people
who can take that seat...

338
00:18:50,930 --> 00:18:52,740
and do a great job.

339
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:56,110
Excuse me? What do you...

340
00:18:56,940 --> 00:18:58,580
What do you mean by that, Mother?

341
00:18:59,040 --> 00:19:01,450
I built this company.

342
00:19:01,550 --> 00:19:03,180
It began with daily loans
and private lending.

343
00:19:03,580 --> 00:19:05,420
I used earnings from dollar trading.

344
00:19:05,920 --> 00:19:07,850
That is how I laid its foundation.

345
00:19:07,850 --> 00:19:11,360
Just because my mind comes and goes,

346
00:19:11,360 --> 00:19:14,590
can you run it however you please?

347
00:19:15,030 --> 00:19:16,960
That is an absurd assumption.

348
00:19:17,590 --> 00:19:19,760
Please tell me what I did wrong.

349
00:19:20,460 --> 00:19:21,830
Our sales for the first half
of this year...

350
00:19:21,900 --> 00:19:23,330
have increased
compared to last year,

351
00:19:23,530 --> 00:19:25,100
so I am not sure
what the problem is.

352
00:19:25,270 --> 00:19:28,210
I saw the list of debtors who owe
hundreds of thousands of dollars.

353
00:19:29,410 --> 00:19:31,140
Why is the collected amount
so small?

354
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:33,080
Looking closely,

355
00:19:33,180 --> 00:19:35,250
even if we push hard
for collection right now,

356
00:19:35,410 --> 00:19:37,950
the amount we can collect
would not be small.

357
00:19:38,150 --> 00:19:39,920
What are you all doing?

358
00:19:40,520 --> 00:19:44,450
For debtors who owe 2,000, 5,000,
or just 10,000 dollars,

359
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:46,820
you harass them so well...

360
00:19:47,320 --> 00:19:49,460
and collect the money so ruthlessly.

361
00:19:50,290 --> 00:19:53,800
What are you trying to do right now?

362
00:19:54,230 --> 00:19:57,200
Mother, that is...

363
00:19:57,270 --> 00:19:59,670
And while you make sure
to give bonuses...

364
00:19:59,840 --> 00:20:00,940
to all the executives and staff,

365
00:20:01,710 --> 00:20:03,870
why do the facility management,
security,

366
00:20:04,070 --> 00:20:06,380
and cleaning staff...

367
00:20:07,140 --> 00:20:08,550
not get any bonuses?

368
00:20:09,850 --> 00:20:12,350
Those employees are
outsourced contractors, so...

369
00:20:14,320 --> 00:20:15,650
You make a mess...

370
00:20:15,720 --> 00:20:17,520
and try to cover it up
with nonsense.

371
00:20:18,390 --> 00:20:20,460
Is that how I raised you?

372
00:20:20,760 --> 00:20:23,130
If you cannot give it to them
because they are outsourced,

373
00:20:23,690 --> 00:20:27,360
hire them directly right now
and give them their bonuses first.

374
00:20:28,870 --> 00:20:30,270
Are you serious, Mother?

375
00:20:30,900 --> 00:20:33,100
If we do that,
the company will lose...

376
00:20:33,170 --> 00:20:35,570
Both you and Jun Sung,
who passed away,

377
00:20:35,840 --> 00:20:37,740
I breastfed you to sleep...

378
00:20:38,240 --> 00:20:41,280
and raised you
while cleaning building restrooms.

379
00:20:41,850 --> 00:20:44,450
I used the money I earned from that
as seed money...

380
00:20:44,820 --> 00:20:46,920
and started daily loans
at the market.

381
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:50,090
Have you forgotten that?

382
00:20:51,150 --> 00:20:54,290
I am sorry, Mother.
I will do as you say.

383
00:20:55,190 --> 00:20:58,260
Yes, I will take care of it
right away.

384
00:20:58,700 --> 00:20:59,700
Yes.

385
00:21:24,020 --> 00:21:26,160
What if she is at work right now?

386
00:21:28,430 --> 00:21:30,930
I guess I will just wait
until evening and come back.

387
00:21:42,070 --> 00:21:43,770
I came because I did not see you
at the store.

388
00:21:44,510 --> 00:21:45,540
My wife.

389
00:21:45,910 --> 00:21:49,210
It has been so long,
but she is still beautiful.

390
00:21:54,890 --> 00:21:55,890
Goodness.

391
00:21:56,190 --> 00:21:57,990
(Security Room)

392
00:22:06,300 --> 00:22:07,530
I am late.

393
00:22:47,140 --> 00:22:48,510
What is that?

394
00:22:50,270 --> 00:22:51,740
Unbelievable.

395
00:22:53,910 --> 00:22:56,450
I am sorry. What do I do?

396
00:22:56,510 --> 00:22:57,510
If I miss this one,

397
00:22:57,580 --> 00:22:59,120
I have to wait 15 minutes.

398
00:23:00,120 --> 00:23:01,120
Ms. Kang Da Mi.

399
00:23:02,190 --> 00:23:03,250
Ms. Kang Da Mi.

400
00:23:04,090 --> 00:23:06,360
- Manager Kang.
- Yes, sir.

401
00:23:06,790 --> 00:23:09,190
What? Who is it?
Who is looking for me on the street?

402
00:23:09,260 --> 00:23:10,290
Manager Kang.

403
00:23:14,830 --> 00:23:17,470
I am off the clock.
Why did you call me?

404
00:23:17,930 --> 00:23:19,540
I called you because
I have business with you.

405
00:23:22,040 --> 00:23:24,570
Why do you have my things?

406
00:23:25,780 --> 00:23:26,910
Where did you get them?

407
00:23:27,440 --> 00:23:28,680
What is with your tone?

408
00:23:28,750 --> 00:23:30,750
You sound like
I stole them or something.

409
00:23:31,010 --> 00:23:32,550
I picked them up over there
on my way.

410
00:23:32,620 --> 00:23:34,680
Why do you drop
your things everywhere?

411
00:23:34,820 --> 00:23:35,920
What are you...

412
00:23:35,990 --> 00:23:37,450
Hansel and Gretel?

413
00:23:38,390 --> 00:23:39,760
Oh my.

414
00:23:42,030 --> 00:23:44,560
Thank you, but I am
a little busy right now.

415
00:23:44,630 --> 00:23:46,560
I have to hurry home
and draw the game board.

416
00:23:46,700 --> 00:23:47,760
I will be going now.

417
00:24:03,950 --> 00:24:07,420
She should at least zip her bag.
Unbelievable.

418
00:24:07,980 --> 00:24:09,290
I thought she was meticulous,

419
00:24:09,350 --> 00:24:11,350
but she is incredibly clumsy,
seriously.

420
00:24:13,620 --> 00:24:15,430
And what is a game board?
A game board?

421
00:24:16,730 --> 00:24:18,090
A game board?

422
00:24:22,600 --> 00:24:24,070
(Game board)

423
00:24:24,670 --> 00:24:25,740
Game Board.

424
00:24:27,140 --> 00:24:28,140
Game...

425
00:24:29,240 --> 00:24:30,770
Game...

426
00:24:34,240 --> 00:24:35,650
What do I do?

427
00:24:35,910 --> 00:24:37,510
It will be a disaster
if Grandma gets angry.

428
00:24:42,390 --> 00:24:45,060
Why do you have my things?

429
00:24:46,190 --> 00:24:47,320
Where did you get them?

430
00:24:47,820 --> 00:24:49,130
What is with your tone?

431
00:24:49,130 --> 00:24:51,160
You sound like
I stole them or something.

432
00:24:51,390 --> 00:24:53,100
I picked them up over there
on my way.

433
00:24:53,160 --> 00:24:55,130
Why do you drop
your things everywhere?

434
00:24:55,230 --> 00:24:56,300
What are you...

435
00:24:56,370 --> 00:24:57,870
Hansel and Gretel?

436
00:25:01,300 --> 00:25:02,310
So embarrassing.

437
00:25:15,650 --> 00:25:17,990
I am glad it is not
a tiny boarding house,

438
00:25:19,220 --> 00:25:21,190
but how can she live
in a place like this alone?

439
00:25:51,350 --> 00:25:53,190
It is too dangerous
for a woman to live alone.

440
00:26:03,370 --> 00:26:04,570
Mother?

441
00:26:08,310 --> 00:26:09,610
How did you...

442
00:26:12,180 --> 00:26:13,540
Da Mi told me.

443
00:26:14,840 --> 00:26:16,450
You must be getting off work now.

444
00:26:18,450 --> 00:26:19,450
Yes.

445
00:26:24,450 --> 00:26:25,460
Let us sit down for a bit.

446
00:26:40,970 --> 00:26:41,970
Are you happy?

447
00:26:42,940 --> 00:26:45,140
Are you? I asked if you are happy.

448
00:26:46,410 --> 00:26:48,550
Your mother is here asking you,
so why can you not say anything?

449
00:26:49,550 --> 00:26:50,550
Tell me.

450
00:26:51,820 --> 00:26:53,080
Get it off your chest and tell me.

451
00:26:59,160 --> 00:27:00,190
Mother.

452
00:27:30,820 --> 00:27:33,620
(Mission: Mompossible)

453
00:27:33,760 --> 00:27:35,190
I do not mean for you
to go to the hotel...

454
00:27:35,260 --> 00:27:38,600
just to work out. You should
naturally build a network...

455
00:27:38,830 --> 00:27:42,330
- with the people who go there.
- Why is the CEO of your company...

456
00:27:42,400 --> 00:27:45,570
trying to set you up with her son?

457
00:27:45,570 --> 00:27:47,070
Did you just say Manager Kang?

458
00:27:47,070 --> 00:27:49,940
Then did that person make
all of these designs?

459
00:27:50,770 --> 00:27:51,780
Interesting.

460
00:27:52,880 --> 00:27:54,880
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
